#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/contrib/cutedsl/atomic/index.rst:40
msgid ""
"Supports float16, float32, int32, and int64 types. Returns the old value "
"before addition (atomicrmw semantics)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/contrib/cutedsl/atomic/index.rst:0
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/contrib/cutedsl/atomic/index.rst:48
msgid ""
"This is the same as AtomicAdd since prims.atomicrmw always returns old value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/contrib/cutedsl/atomic/index.rst:55
msgid ""
"Follows ``AtomicAddx2`` in ``src/tl_templates/cuda/atomic.h``: float16 and "
"bfloat16 use one packed ``f16x2`` / ``bf16x2`` atomic (a CAS loop for bf16 "
"below sm_90), which also works on shared memory; float32 uses "
"``atom.global.add.v2.f32`` on sm_90+ and two scalar atomics below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/contrib/cutedsl/atomic/index.rst:60
#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/contrib/cutedsl/atomic/index.rst:74
msgid "Pointer to destination (2 consecutive elements)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/contrib/cutedsl/atomic/index.rst:61
#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/contrib/cutedsl/atomic/index.rst:75
#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/contrib/cutedsl/atomic/index.rst:88
#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/contrib/cutedsl/atomic/index.rst:103
msgid "Source values - can be TensorSSA (loaded tensor) or Pointer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/contrib/cutedsl/atomic/index.rst:68
msgid "Follows ``AtomicAddx2Ret`` in ``src/tl_templates/cuda/atomic.h``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/contrib/cutedsl/atomic/index.rst:70
msgid ""
"float16/bfloat16: one packed ``f16x2`` / ``bf16x2`` atomic (a CAS loop for "
"bf16 below sm_90) with generic addressing, so shared memory works too."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/contrib/cutedsl/atomic/index.rst:72
msgid ""
"float32: one ``atom.global.add.v2.f32`` on sm_90+, two scalar atomics below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/contrib/cutedsl/atomic/index.rst:82
msgid ""
"Follows ``AtomicAddx4`` in ``src/tl_templates/cuda/atomic.h``. On sm_90+ it "
"is one ``atom.global`` vector atomic (``v4.f32`` or ``v4.{f16,bf16}``); "
"below that, float32 becomes four scalar atomics and 16-bit types two packed "
"pair atomics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/contrib/cutedsl/atomic/index.rst:87
#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/contrib/cutedsl/atomic/index.rst:102
msgid "Pointer to destination (4 consecutive elements)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/contrib/cutedsl/atomic/index.rst:95
msgid "Follows ``AtomicAddx4Ret`` in ``src/tl_templates/cuda/atomic.h``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/contrib/cutedsl/atomic/index.rst:97
msgid ""
"float32: one ``atom.global.add.v4.f32`` on sm_90+, four scalar atomics below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/contrib/cutedsl/atomic/index.rst:98
msgid ""
"float16/bfloat16: no x4 atomic exists, so two packed pair atomics "
"(``f16x2`` / ``bf16x2``; a CAS loop for bf16 below sm_90). The 8-byte "
"destination is never written as 16 bytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/contrib/cutedsl/atomic/index.rst:110
msgid ""
"For integers, uses prims.atomicrmw with MAX. For floats, uses CAS loop since "
"PTX doesn't have atomic max for float32."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/contrib/cutedsl/atomic/index.rst:123
msgid ""
"For integers, uses prims.atomicrmw with MIN. For floats, uses CAS loop since "
"PTX doesn't have atomic min for float32."
msgstr ""

